.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH taur-serve 1  "taur-serve " 
.SH NAME
taur\-serve \- Run the HTTP server (AUR RPC, git, snapshots, dumps, API) and optional SSH server
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaur serve\fR [\fB\-\-bind\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-ssh\-bind\fR] [\fB\-\-base\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-smtp\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-mail\-from\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the HTTP server (AUR RPC, git, snapshots, dumps, API) and optional SSH server
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-bind\fR \fI<BIND>\fR [default: 127.0.0.1:8080]

.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
Data directory (default: $TAUR_HOME, else ~/.local/share/taur)
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh\-bind\fR \fI<SSH_BIND>\fR
Also serve git over SSH on this address (e.g. 0.0.0.0:2222)
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<BASE_URL>\fR [default: https://taur.weirdbrains.com]
Public base URL used in email links
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_BASE_URL\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-smtp\-url\fR \fI<SMTP_URL>\fR
SMTP server URL, e.g. smtps://user:pass@smtp.example.com (never logged). Without it, mail is written to <home>/outbox
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SMTP_URL\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-mail\-from\fR \fI<MAIL_FROM>\fR [default: TAUR <noreply@taur.weirdbrains.com>]
Sender address for outgoing mail
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_MAIL_FROM\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
